---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import headshot from '../assets/Taylor_headshot.png';
---

<Base
  title="About | Taylormade Brands"
  description="Josh Taylor and Taylormade Brands — a growth partner for owner-led businesses, combining custom software, strategy, research, and marketing with a background in leadership and systems."
>
  <main>
    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="ink page-hero grid-bg glow-gold">
      <div class="container wide">
        <div class="hero-split">
          <div>
            <p class="label">About</p>
            <h1 class="display">A partner in the business, not a vendor to it.</h1>
            <p class="lead muted">
              I help owner-led businesses run better and grow — with custom software, clear strategy,
              honest research, and marketing that actually connects. One person accountable for the
              whole picture.
            </p>
            <div class="btn-row mt-m">
              <a href="/growth-assessment.html" class="btn btn-primary">Start an assessment <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
              <a href="/work.html" class="btn btn-ghost">See the work</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="about-card card reveal">
            <div class="about-photo"><Image src={headshot} alt="Josh Taylor" width={560} /></div>
            <div class="about-id">
              <h3>Josh Taylor</h3>
              <p class="label plain">Founder · Taylormade Brands</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- STORY -->
    <section class="paper section">
      <div class="container wide split">
        <div>
          <p class="label">Why it exists</p>
          <h2>Good businesses lose ground when their systems can't keep up.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="story-body">
          <p>I kept seeing the same thing: owners doing excellent work, held back not by the work itself but by everything around it — a website that undersold them, a Google presence that was invisible, and operations still living in a notebook or a dozen spreadsheets.</p>
          <p>Taylormade Brands started as branding and websites. But the businesses I worked with kept needing more — a way to capture leads, a system to run the day, real numbers to make decisions. So the work grew into what it is now: custom software, strategy, research, and reporting, alongside the marketing.</p>
          <p>That's the difference between a vendor and a partner. A vendor hands you a deliverable. A partner stays in the business with you and builds what it actually needs next.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- APPROACH -->
    <section class="ink section">
      <div class="container wide">
        <div class="head">
          <p class="label">How I work</p>
          <h2>Systems beat scattered effort.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid-4">
          <div class="card num-card reveal"><span class="index">01</span><h3>Understand first</h3><p class="muted">Before building anything, I learn how the business really runs and where growth is leaking.</p></div>
          <div class="card num-card reveal"><span class="index">02</span><h3>Build the system</h3><p class="muted">Software, brand, and lead flow designed to work together and remove the busywork.</p></div>
          <div class="card num-card reveal"><span class="index">03</span><h3>Measure honestly</h3><p class="muted">Research and reporting so decisions are made on evidence, and you can see what's working.</p></div>
          <div class="card num-card reveal"><span class="index">04</span><h3>Grow together</h3><p class="muted">We iterate as a partnership, and the system compounds over time.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- BACKGROUND -->
    <section class="paper section">
      <div class="container wide split">
        <div>
          <p class="label">Background</p>
          <h2>Leadership and systems, before software.</h2>
          <p class="lead muted mt-s">My path isn't traditional agency work. It comes from education leadership, coaching, ministry, and community — years spent building systems, leading teams, and solving practical problems. That's what shapes how I partner with businesses today.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card bg-list reveal">
          <h4>Experience that shapes the work</h4>
          <ul class="check-list mt-m">
            <li>Education leadership and statewide systems work</li>
            <li>Former school administrator</li>
            <li>Youth sports coach and local league volunteer</li>
            <li>Ministry leadership and teaching</li>
            <li>Community-based relationship building</li>
            <li>Process improvement and practical problem solving</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- LOCAL -->
    <section class="ink-2 section">
      <div class="container narrow center">
        <p class="label center mx-auto">Local roots</p>
        <h2 class="mt-s">I care about local businesses because I care about local communities.</h2>
        <p class="lead muted mt-m mx-auto" style="max-width:64ch;">I grew up in this area, raise my family here, coach here, and serve here. Small businesses aren't logos on a screen — they're families, jobs, and community trust. I don't build things to look good in a portfolio. I build them to help real businesses earn attention, build trust, and create opportunities.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FIT -->
    <section class="paper section">
      <div class="container wide">
        <div class="head center mx-auto">
          <p class="label center mx-auto">Who I work best with</p>
          <h2>Owners who want a partner and clear next steps.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid-3">
          <div class="card num-card"><h3>Local service businesses</h3><p class="muted">Trades, contractors, farms, and owner-led companies that do great work and want it to show.</p></div>
          <div class="card num-card"><h3>Teams &amp; organizations</h3><p class="muted">Leagues, teams, churches, schools, and nonprofits that need a stronger presence and better systems.</p></div>
          <div class="card num-card"><h3>Growing businesses</h3><p class="muted">Companies that have outgrown spreadsheets and off-the-shelf tools and need something built for them.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="ink section">
      <div class="container narrow center">
        <p class="label center mx-auto">Start here</p>
        <h2 class="mt-s">Let's talk about where your business is headed.</h2>
        <p class="lead muted mt-s mx-auto" style="max-width:54ch;">Take the growth assessment and I'll review where you are, what's missing, and the best place to start.</p>
        <div class="btn-row mt-m" style="justify-content:center;">
          <a href="/growth-assessment.html" class="btn btn-primary">Start assessment <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
          <a href="/contact.html" class="btn btn-ghost">Contact me</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    .about-card { padding: 0; overflow: hidden; }
    .about-photo :global(img) { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
    .about-id { padding: 22px 26px 26px; }
    .about-id h3 { margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .story-body p { margin-bottom: 18px; }
    .story-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .paper .story-body p { color: var(--l-muted); }
    .bg-list h4 { font-size: 1.15rem; }
    @media (max-width: 900px) { .split, .hero-split { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .grid-3, .grid-4 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
    @media (min-width: 561px) and (max-width: 900px) { .grid-4 { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  </style>
</Base>
